<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  `direct` flavor manifest — merged only into the sideloaded build.

  Everything here is something Google Play would take issue with, so it lives in this
  source set and can never leak into the `play` AAB.

  1. REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES lets UpdatePlugin hand a downloaded APK to the system
     installer. That is the whole point of the direct build and is flatly prohibited
     for anything distributed through Google Play (Device and Network Abuse policy).

  2. ReminderCarAppService is the Android Auto car screen. A templated car app must
     declare one of Auto's approved categories, and a reminder app is none of them
     (navigation / parking / charging / POI / IOT / settings / messaging / calling /
     weather), so shipping it in the Play build would put every release at risk of an
     Auto review rejection for the sake of a screen. SETTINGS is the closest fit of a
     bad set and is what the sideloaded build declares. See docs/alarm-architecture.md
     and store/play-readiness.md.

  3. **The Android Auto notification declaration.** `com.google.android.gms.car.application`
     sat in src/main for months on the reasoning that mirroring nags into the car "needs
     no category". It needs no category, but what it said was `<uses name="notification"/>`,
     and the only thing that means to Auto is "this app sends and receives short-form
     messages". Play's Auto review correctly found that a
     reminder app can do neither, which is the 2026-08-17 policy notice.

     That claim is gone: the file now says `<uses name="template"/>`, because notifications
     never needed the messaging route. `CarAppExtender` is what makes Auto display one, and
     it carries its own Done/Snooze actions. So the declaration is honest again, and it is
     direct-only for note 2's reason instead: `template` and the CarAppService are one
     claim, and that claim needs a category. `res/xml/automotive_app_desc.xml` moves with
     it (setup-android.mjs copies it into this flavor's res/, not src/main's): a resource
     the entry points at is part of the same declaration.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!-- androidx.car.app is minSdk 23 while the app floor is 22. Android Auto itself
         needs API 23+, and CarProjection.init is SDK-guarded, so this override belongs
         only to the flavor that carries the library. -->
    <uses-sdk tools:overrideLibrary="androidx.car.app" />

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES" />

    <application>
        <!-- Car API level 1 is all the list/message templates this app uses need, so it
             stays compatible with the widest set of head units. -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="androidx.car.app.minCarApiLevel"
            android:value="1" />

        <!-- Declares this build to Android Auto; points at
             res/xml/automotive_app_desc.xml (<uses name="template"/>). Direct-only.
             See notes 2 and 3 above. -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.car.application"
            android:resource="@xml/automotive_app_desc" />

        <service
            android:name="ca.persistent.app.alarm.ReminderCarAppService"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.car.app.CarAppService" />
                <category android:name="androidx.car.app.category.SETTINGS" />
            </intent-filter>
        </service>
    </application>
</manifest>
